<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emilio De Bono</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emilio De Bono was an Italian general and one of the four leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-on-rome">March on Rome</a> in 1922. He served as governor of Tripolitania and minister of the colonies, and in October 1935 commanded the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-badoglio">Pietro Badoglio</a> replaced him in November. In July 1943 he voted against Mussolini in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-of-fascism">Fascist Grand Council</a>, and he was tried and shot at Verona by the Italian Social Republic in January 1944.</p></div>
